  "caption": "Quinn started a 10-minute plank plan and braced the belly all day long. The back still ached. Rude.\n\nHere's the twist: back pain usually isn't caused by a 'weak core'. Studies suggest dedicated core programs work about as well as general exercise, and your spine is sturdier than it gets credit for.\n\nWhat often helps: choose progressive exercise you'll actually keep doing, let squats, deadlifts and loaded carries train your trunk, and skip constant bracing in daily life. Sleep, stress and overall activity matter too. Planks are welcome if you enjoy them.\n\nBack pain with leg pain, numbness or weakness is worth a proper assessment.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
